  "id": "ceft",
  "term": "CEFT",
  "definition": "CEFT refers to ceftiofur, one of the antimicrobial treatments studied for metaphylaxis, meaning mass preventive antibiotic use when cattle arrive at a feedlot. In this study, the CEFT group showed changes in blood gene expression linked to immune-related pathways, suggesting immunomodulatory as well as antimicrobial effects.",
